{"diagnosis": "SLTIU test expects x3=1 for unsigned compare 5000 < 0xFFFFFFFF (-1 sign-extended) but DUT stored datao=0x00000000 instead of 0x00000001. Zero-extended UIMM turns 0xFFF into 4095, so 5000<4095 evaluates false. Root cause is line 531 where U2REGX selects UIMM instead of sign-extended SIMM bits for the I-type unsigned operand.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/rtl/darkriscv.v b/rtl/darkriscv.v
--- a/rtl/darkriscv.v
+++ b/rtl/darkriscv.v
@@ -528,7 +528,7 @@
     // RM-group of instructions (OPCODEs==7'b0010011/7'b0110011), merged! src=immediate(M)/register(R)

     wire signed [31:0] S2REGX = XMCC ? SIMM : S2REG;
-    wire        [31:0] U2REGX = XMCC ? UIMM : U2REG;
+    wire        [31:0] U2REGX = XMCC ? SIMM : U2REG;

 `ifdef __MEXT__
", "expected": "tohost: PASS with store daddr=00000000 datao=00000001"}

